1.24,"s":"hybrid/balanced-advantage and multi-asset funds that actively fight an aggressive, >20%-expectation, wealth-creation mandate."},{"x":45.35,"end":589.09,"y":299.34,"s":"• A full cleanup (\"Path A\") would realize Rs. 8,82,012 of gains and cost ~Rs. 94,626 in LTCG tax. You asked to cap tax at Rs. 30,000 — so this plan"},{"x":52.28,"end":439.53,"y":287.43,"s":"is split into two phases using two separate financial years' Rs. 1,25,000 LTCG exemptions instead of one."},{"x":45.35,"end":563.1,"y":275.53,"s":"• PHASE 1 (now): Exit 14 positions — every dead-weight/duplicate fund except the single largest tax bomb. Total gain realized: Rs. 332,194."},{"x":52.28,"end":548.41,"y":263.62,"s":"Taxable after this FY's exemption: Rs. 207,194. Estimated LTCG tax: Rs. 25,899 — under the Rs. 30,000 cap, with headroom to spare."},{"x":45.35,"end":585.24,"y":251.72,"s":"• PHASE 2 (after 1-Apr-2027, fresh exemption): the HDFC Balanced Advantage Regular position (Rs. 2,85,895 MV, Rs. 171,895 gain alone) and 4"},{"x":52.28,"end":617.3,"y":239.81,"s":"Regular-to-Direct switch-throughs (Axis Midcap, HSBC Midcap x2, Motilal Oswal Flexi Cap — all with dormant SIPs) are held as-is and dealt with next FY."},{"x":52.28,"end":591.09,"y":227.91,"s":"Cost of waiting: a few more months of Regular-plan expense drag (~0.5-1%/yr) on ~Rs. 9.62L — a small, known cost versus paying tax on it today."},{"x":45.35,"end":530.35,"y":216,"s":"• Phase 1 proceeds (Rs. 1,499,194) minus the tax reserve (Rs. 25,899) leave Rs. 1,473,295 to redeploy. This was run through a full"},{"x":52.28,"end":614.36,"y":204.09,"s":"JAGERBOMB pass (ratings + 1Y/3Y/5Y performance vs category) before finalizing: Bandhan Small Cap (Rs. 5,23,295, largest share) clearly outperforms"},{"x":52.28,"end":582.71,"y":192.19,"s":"Nippon Small Cap on every risk-adjusted metric (3Y 23.0% vs 14.5%, Sharpe 0.87 vs 0.52), so Nippon's top-up was trimmed in Bandhan's favor."},{"x":52.28,"end":586.62,"y":180.28,"s":"Motilal Oswal Midcap's rating fell to 3-star with a NEGATIVE 1-year return (-2.79%) — a rating-downgrade/momentum flag — so it gets zero fresh"},{"x":52.28,"end":600.3,"y":168.38,"s":"money (lumpsum or SIP), existing Rs. 85,269 held as-is. HSBC Midcap (5-star, 1Y 17.4%) is the strongest midcap here but is capped at Rs. 2,00,000"},{"x":52.28,"end":592.44,"y":156.47,"s":"purely for AMC concentration (2 deferred Regular folios already sit in HSBC). A new Large & Mid Cap anchor (ICICI Pru, Rs. 1,50,000) restores the"},{"x":52.28,"end":595.91,"y":144.57,"s":"large-cap exposure Phase 1's exits removed — flagged for a weak recent 1Y return, but sized as ballast, not a return driver, staying well under 20%."},{"x":45.35,"end":555.73,"y":132.66,"s":"• SIP stays at Rs. 45,000/month total — 6 SIPs feeding exited/flagged funds are stopped (including PPFAS and Motilal Oswal Midcap) and"},{"x":52.28,"end":601.2,"y":120.76,"s":"redirected into Edelweiss Mid Cap (Rs.9,000), Bandhan Small Cap (Rs.13,000), HSBC Midcap (Rs.4,000) and ICICI Pru Large & Mid Cap (Rs.4,000)."},{"x":52.28,"end":441.17,"y":108.85,"s":"The 3 SIPs feeding good-fit Direct funds (ABSL PSU, ICICI Infra, Nippon Small Cap) continue unchanged."},{"x":45.35,"end":600.71,"y":96.94,"s":"• A note on the >20% return expectation: realistic only in strong bull-market years, not as a dependable long-term planning assumption. The Base case"},{"x":52.28,"end":585.75,"y":85.04,"s":"below (~15% CAGR) is what this plan is actually built around; Moonshot (~21%) shows what's possible in a strong cycle, not what to plan around."},{"x":45.35,"end":247.93,"y":22.68,"s":"Univest Wealth Portfolio Report — Sample Client Three — Page 1"},{"x":607.7,"end":796.54,"y":22.68,"s":"Prepared by Univest Wealth — SEBI RIA INA000017639"}]},{"page":2,"items":[{"x":45.35,"end":82.19,"y":569.76,"s":"UNIVEST"},{"x":87.87,"end":123.29,"y":569.76,"s":"WEALTH"},{"x":45.35,"end":251.17,"y":555.59,"s":"14 POSITIONS, RS. 332,194 GAIN, TAX CAPPED AT RS. 25,899"},{"x":45.35,"end":211